WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.755 --> 00:00:03.338
(film reeling)

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.090
(dramatic music)

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.693
- I want you to say something.

00:00:10.693 --> 00:00:11.640
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.473
You ready?

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:18.156
This is a giant map of Switzerland.

00:00:18.156 --> 00:00:20.180
(choir like music)

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.250
I love Switzerland.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.390
And one thing I have
learned about Switzerland

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.250
is that the Swiss like to be neutral.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.833
(somber music)

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:34.860
This country does not like conflict.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.990
They avoid it at all costs,

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.250
which is strange because
they're really good at fighting.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.790
Other European countries
used to hire Swiss men

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:44.280
to fight their wars for them.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.090
But back home in Switzerland,
they don't fight.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:48.220
They don't take sides.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.070
That's partly because they
lost a few wars of expansion

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.230
and kind of just decided
it was probably better

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:54.300
to just stay put.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.550
But it's also because back when
Europe was full of empires,

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.940
the big European powers
thought it would be a good idea

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.840
to have a mountainous small buffer country

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.020
in between some of the big rival powers.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:08.930
And so Switzerland was kind
of deemed this neutral power,

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:13.370
but the result is that today
Switzerland doesn't take sides.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:15.830
They don't send their troops
to fight another other wars.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.970
They rarely join alliances.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.820
I mean, they're not a part of the EU.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.140
They're not a part of NATO.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.260
And they reluctantly barely joined the UN

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:28.620
as recently as 2002, a
decade after North Korea.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.570
And the only countries
that joined after them

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.670
didn't exist before then.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.770
Meaning they came into
existence after 2002.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.250
So they couldn't have joined before then.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.100
Switzerland is serious about neutrality,

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.110
no conflict, no alliances.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.093
Leave us alone.

00:01:42.093 --> 00:01:43.330
(somber music)

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:44.820
When you're right here,

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.490
right at the crossroads of people

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:47.890
trying to take over Europe,

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.430
staying out of conflict has
big benefits for your country

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:51.430
and its economy.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:54.800
But it also means staying
neutral is really hard,

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.370
but the Swiss have done it.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.140
Using their mountains, some
exceptional engineering,

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.400
obsessive commitment,

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.250
and a healthy amount of explosives.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.420
The Swiss have kept empires
out of their country,

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:06.520
sticking to their guns

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.670
and staying neutral

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:10.039
even when Europe was tearing itself apart.

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:12.622
(somber music)

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:18.490
So you're Switzerland in the 1940s.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.010
Here's your situation.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.570
You're surrounded by Nazi
Germany to your North

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.140
and Fascist Italy to your South

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.000
and quickly are becoming engulfed

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.170
with all the countries
that are now in the sphere

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.490
of influence of these countries.

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:34.600
You're surrounded and Hitler
is winning everywhere,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.520
but you're Switzerland.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.650
And so you're like, don't invade us.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.290
We're not going to fight,
we're not taking sides.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:42.210
We'll just keep trading with
whoever wants to trade with us,

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.030
but we're not going to fight

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.030
or be invaded.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.750
And no, that's not how
Europe was in the 1940s.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.110
You couldn't just sit it out.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:53.020
And yet the Swiss were
committed to doing so.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:56.670
The fact is that even with
this commitment to neutrality

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.640
an invasion from their next door neighbor,

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.520
the Third Reich, was it
very real possibility.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:04.480
So Switzerland devised, what I argue

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.100
is just the most Swiss plan ever.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.270
To stay neutral during World War II

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:10.830
and future global conflicts.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.000
It's a plan that still lives on today

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.500
that you can still see
when you go to Switzerland.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.913
Here's what it looks like.

00:03:16.913 --> 00:03:19.580
(upbeat music)

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.420
First up, hey looked around their country

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.710
at any linkages to the outside.

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:26.570
They choose key points around the country

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:29.410
that would give invading
armies access to the country

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:31.260
like roads, bridges, tunnels,

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.210
any access point.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:35.250
And then they packed
it full of explosives.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.170
(explosion noise)

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.990
Dynamite, TNT, whatever.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:42.410
Anything that would just
completely destroy that linkage.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.030
They got really inventive with this stuff.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.320
Sometimes they would wire
a bridge with dynamite,

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.533
but they also would put
secret canons in mountains

00:03:48.533 --> 00:03:49.560
that would pop out

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.160
and point at a major road

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.470
and demolish it if needed,

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:53.870
making it unusable.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.150
Or sometimes they would
go to their long tunnels

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.790
like this 10 kilometer tunnel down here

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:59.040
at the border with Italy.

00:04:00.066 --> 00:04:00.899
And they would rig it with TNT

00:04:00.899 --> 00:04:02.900
so that they could
quickly seal off this part

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.825
of their mountainous Southern border.

00:04:04.825 --> 00:04:08.170
(ominous music)

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:10.090
Up on mountain passes they even rigged

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.980
the sides of mountains with explosives

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.290
to create artificial
landslides to block the road.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:17.440
The thinking here is
that if an invading army

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.930
were marching into Switzerland,

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.940
they could pull the
trigger on all this stuff.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.690
Igniting dynamite or shelling

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.060
or otherwise destroying all the ways

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.070
to get into the country,

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.870
making it a lot harder to invade

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.420
and giving them time to
retreat to the mountains.

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:33.610
There's a wonderful,
strange irony going on here.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.800
The Swiss are really
good at transportation.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.710
The trains are immaculate and efficient

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.290
and go up crazy mountains

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.810
and are always on time.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.170
Roam around the country
and you'll see this.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.580
These are the little doors in the streets

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.170
where they would pack explosives.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:50.370
So it's kind of ironic that
all of this infrastructure

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.790
was packed with explosives,

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.140
but I guess that makes
it even more functional

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.691
because now it's a defense mechanism.

00:04:57.691 --> 00:05:01.360
In addition to being
infrastructure for transportation.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.132
I love Switzerland.

00:05:03.132 --> 00:05:05.632
(jet engines)

00:05:06.969 --> 00:05:09.552
(somber music)

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.780
There's this one bridge that
connects Switzerland to Germany

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:16.570
that was built in 2006.

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:19.370
And when it was built, it
was packed with explosives.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:22.050
This bridge was built in
conjunction with Germany.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.130
Germany paved half of the bridge,

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.120
and yet they didn't even
know that it was rigged

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.280
with explosives.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.910
It's very aggressive Switzerland.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:29.760
Okay, so anyway.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.980
Blowing up their borders
and sealing themselves off

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:35.820
was one major strategy for
aggressively staying neutral.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.526
Let's get onto the next one.

00:05:37.526 --> 00:05:39.690
(dramatic music)

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.810
Zoom into the lower half of Switzerland.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.840
And you'll be struck by one massive thing

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.290
that Switzerland has.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:46.400
Mountains.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.120
Big, giant mountains that flank across

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.620
the South part of the country.

00:05:51.814 --> 00:05:52.647
(dramatic music)

00:05:52.647 --> 00:05:53.850
Another thing Swiss was have

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:58.410
is an unmatched ability to
drill holes into mountains.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.450
The country has over a thousand tunnels.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.730
One of which is 57 kilometers long.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:07.750
These people know how to
build holes in mountains.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.630
And that skill becomes very useful

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:13.303
when your situation looks like this.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:16.600
Most of the population lives here,

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.410
meaning not in the mountains.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.560
And so there wasn't much of a separation

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.400
between these population centers

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.160
and Nazi Germany.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.700
After the Swiss saw
Hitler march into Paris

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.910
and take over huge portions of France,

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.030
they got serious about figuring out

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.560
what they would do if Hitler invaded.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:35.550
So they had their plan
to blow up the borders

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.710
and slow down an invasion.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.000
But where could they retreat to

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.630
that would allow them to stay neutral

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:43.570
and stay alive during the fighting?

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:46.670
In the mountains, they were
building giant fortresses

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.580
and bunkers and tunnels

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.820
that work literally inside of the Alps.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.390
They built thousands of these things

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.380
in the side of mountains,

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.250
and they rigged them with guns,

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.520
and cannons,

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.430
as well as full on bases

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:02.570
that were equipped with supplies and beds

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.430
and living space.

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:07.200
Sometimes they'd be hidden
in steep mountain passes,

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.700
disguised as a barn,

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.240
but really it would be a bunker

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.190
with hidden explosives, supplies,

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:13.720
and men ready to fight.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:17.140
All over the Alps, the Swiss
built these secret bunkers

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:18.460
mainly during World War II

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.660
in preparation for any sort of invasion.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.340
Once the war ended, the
idea of putting bunkers

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:24.850
in the mountains for defense

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:27.170
and neutrality became pretty embedded

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.970
in the Swiss security doctrine,

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:31.169
as well as just Swiss culture.

00:07:31.169 --> 00:07:33.350
(upbeat music)

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:35.100
So I did a call out on Instagram stories

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.870
to see if this bunker
culture was still a thing.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:41.350
And I caught a lot of
responses that showed me

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:44.970
that it's not just World
War II in the mountains.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:48.502
Swiss bunkers are all over the country.

00:07:48.502 --> 00:07:51.070
(upbeat music)

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.340
Geez.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.400
That's a lot of bunkers.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.460
Thank you to all of those

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:56.300
who sent me pictures of your bunkers.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.900
After World War II, the new
threat was the Soviet Union

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:00.910
and the Cold War

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.470
and nuclear destruction.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:05.820
Bunkers were now built into
homes, apartment buildings,

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:09.150
hospitals, public
infrastructure of all kind

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.710
had bunkers underneath it.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.400
By the 1960s, Switzerland had built enough

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.210
underground bunkers and shelters

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:17.550
to protect the entire population

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.910
and with a healthy surplus.

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.270
Something that no other
country's ever done.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.103
Okay.

00:08:23.103 --> 00:08:24.700
So let's talk about the last step here,

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:27.347
which is kind of the dark
side of Swiss neutrality

00:08:27.347 --> 00:08:29.860
and the one that no one
really wants to talk about,

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.628
but gotta talk about it.

00:08:31.628 --> 00:08:34.040
(ominous music)

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.460
So let me reiterate here

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.930
that staying neutral and safe

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:41.660
when this is your situation
is a very difficult thing.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:45.020
I mean, World War II was
an incredible tragedy

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.480
where millions of people lost their lives.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:49.383
During World War II,

00:08:49.383 --> 00:08:51.530
Switzerland had an official
policy of neutrality.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:54.830
This meant that they
would trade with whomever.

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:57.360
Whether it was the Axis and Hitler,

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:59.820
or it was the Allies and Churchill.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:03.350
But in reality, Switzerland
traded a lot more with Germany,

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:06.180
providing them with anti-aircraft guns

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:09.280
and other military supplies and ammunition

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.930
that was used in the war.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:14.470
In addition, Switzerland
allowed the Nazi regime

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.670
to store lots of gold and art

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:20.360
and other valuables that
were looted from victims

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.450
of the war.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.360
And specifically the Holocaust.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.140
Not a super good look.

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:28.260
Defenders of this will
tell you that Switzerland

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:30.850
was doing what it needed to
do to stay out of the war,

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:32.170
to stay neutral

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.200
and just like blowing up your borders

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.650
or making bunkers in the mountains.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:38.880
This pandering to Hitler

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:41.780
and being kind of on decent
terms with the Third Reich

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:45.160
was a way of making it more costly

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.570
and more implausible that Germany

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:51.230
would just pop right down
South from where they are

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.860
to take over this small country.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.600
Neutrality does not mean holding hands

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.330
and singing kumbaya.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:01.900
Neutrality in the Swiss
foreign policy doctrine

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:04.610
means deterrence and defense.

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:07.177
There's a Swiss military saying that says,

00:10:07.177 --> 00:10:11.119
"In order to remain in peace,
you have to have cannons."

00:10:11.119 --> 00:10:13.869
(artillery fire)

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:17.450
This kind of sums it up.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.730
Not only did they have
cannons and weaponry,

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:22.520
but they also played by
whatever rules they needed to

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:24.890
in order to stay out of the war.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.440
And it worked.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:30.030
Hitler had a pretty developed
plan to take over Switzerland,

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.400
but in the end it didn't
make strategic sense.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.840
It was too costly and implausible for them

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:38.415
to take over their neighbor to the South.

00:10:38.415 --> 00:10:39.890
Even though he had taken over the majority

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:41.720
of the European continent at that point.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:43.710
I would bet a large sum of money

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:45.820
that the top comment on this video

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:48.420
is someone badmouthing the Swiss

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.700
for all of this World War II stuff.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:51.533
Which, whatever.

00:10:51.533 --> 00:10:52.960
I don't have a dog in this fight.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.912
If that's how you feel,
that's how you feel.

00:10:55.912 --> 00:10:59.300
(somber music)

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.387
Okay.

00:11:00.387 --> 00:11:03.390
So these two massive global wars are over

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:05.640
and Switzerland is still neutral,

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.950
but they don't have to
take as extreme measures

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:09.250
to remain so.

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:12.030
So what do you do with all these bunkers?

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:14.210
First, the bombing the borders thing,

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:16.850
where they packed explosives
in all of these bridges

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:18.670
and roads and tunnels.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:21.630
It turns out that the military
slowly started to dismantle

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:23.410
all of this a few years ago.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.550
And by 2014, the military says

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:29.640
that all of the mines and bombs and TNT

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.990
have been removed from
public infrastructure.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:33.350
Good for you military.

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:34.910
No more bombs at bridges.

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:36.240
So for the household bunkers

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.800
that were built during the Cold War,

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:38.633
those are still there.

00:11:38.633 --> 00:11:40.030
And my friends on Instagram tell me

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:42.920
that they're just kind of
used for like storage rooms

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.920
or sometimes like as a laundry room.

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:46.430
Extra space, I guess,

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.230
with really fortified doors

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:51.410
that will withstand the
radioactivity of a nuclear weapon.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.130
I mean, it's not bad to have.

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:54.420
But what I'm really interested in

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.450
is all of the mountain fortresses

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:57.350
and tunnels,

00:11:57.350 --> 00:12:00.020
and like bunkers that
were in the Swiss Alps.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:01.200
What happened to those?

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.110
Those were really expensive to build

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:04.870
and were expensive to maintain.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.150
And the military is honestly kind of eager

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:08.180
to get rid of them.

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:09.570
Some of them have been sold off

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:11.930
and turned into like fancy hotels

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:13.230
in the side of a mountain.

00:12:14.431 --> 00:12:16.450
Others are used as cheese sellers

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.400
to make delicious Swiss cheese.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:19.640
And then you've got this one,

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:22.580
which was purchased by like
a tech security company

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:25.860
that specializes in
keeping your data safe.

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:27.510
So you can store your Bitcoin

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:28.810
or whatever else you need

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:30.880
on these super secure servers

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.410
in the side of a Swiss mountain.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.660
They claim these servers are so protected

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:38.140
that they are impervious even
to an electromagnetic shock

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:39.320
from an atom bomb.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.140
It seems to me like a little bit overkill,

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:44.010
but if you have some
really important documents

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:46.090
and files that you need to save,

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:47.050
this is your place.

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:48.640
But the majority of these mountain bunkers

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:51.780
and fortresses lie completely abandoned.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.400
If you hike around Switzerland,

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:55.870
you will see these things everywhere,

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.780
which is something I've never done.

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:00.180
And really now want to do.

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:02.330
Go like bunker hunting in Switzerland.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:03.450
It sounds kind of amazing.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.430
All right, so the Swiss stayed neutral.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:06.640
They've continued to stay neutral.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:08.790
They will probably
continue to stay neutral

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:11.700
and it turns out that we'll
use whatever means necessary

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.100
to do so.

